    "description": {
      "value": "<p>Your companion is a lean, snub-nosed rodent popular among goblins as a mount.</p><p><strong>Size</strong> Medium</p><p><strong>Melee</strong> <span class=\"pf2-icon\">1</span> jaws, Damage 1d6 piercing</p><p><strong>Str</strong> +3, <strong>Con</strong> +2, <strong>Dex</strong> +2, <strong>Int</strong> –4, <strong>Wis</strong> +1, <strong>Cha</strong> +0</p><p><strong>Hit Points</strong> 6</p><p><strong>Skill</strong> Stealth</p><p><strong>Speed</strong> 40 feet</p><p><strong>Special</strong> mount; when a goblin dog becomes a mature animal companion, you can choose for it to remain Medium</p><p><strong>Support Benefit</strong> Your goblin dog scratches itself, spreading itchy dander. Until the start of your next turn, if you hit and deal damage to a creature within your goblin dog's reach, the creature is @UUID[Compendium.sf2e.conditions.Item.fesd1n5eVhpCSS18]{Sickened 1} until the start of your next turn or until it Interacts to brush off the dander.</p><p><strong>Advanced Maneuver</strong> @UUID[Compendium.pf2e-animal-companions.sf-AC-Advanced-Maneuvers.Item.AmMy9Oe71Zpo2n7b]{Slobbering Bite}</p>",
